Historical Events: Before the conquest of Muslim, Rangamati region was a contesting ground
between the kings of the Tripura and the Arakan. In 1666, this region came under the Mughals. It was
leased to the English East India Company in 1760-61. In 1737, one tribal leader SherMosta Khan took
refuge with the Mughals. Since then, the Chakmas settled in this region who were followed by other
ethnic communities.
Ethnic Communities: Ethnic communities such as Chakma, Marma, Tanchangya, Tripura, Chak,
Khumee, Luchei, Pankhoa, Riang, Khumi, Mro, Sant al, Monipuri, Bome, Kheyang, Murang and other
sub-groups belong to this zila.
Temperature and Rainfall: The annual average temperature of the zila varies maximum 34.6°C to

